-Java Program Structure:
------------------------
package statements             --> Optional/On demand, Replacement for header file
import statements.             --> Optional/On demand basis
class declaration              --> Our plan/what we are going to do, our action(Logic starts here)
variables                      --> used to store the data
methods                        --> Used to perform actions

Java is case sensitive, we need to follow syntax

-Translators: It is used to convert from one format to other format
------------
3 types of translators available
1. Interpreter  -> It will convert program line by line (Performance is low)
2. Compiler     -> It will convert all the lines of program (Performance is fast)
3. Assembler    -> It is used to convert assembler programming language into machine language.

Note: Java using both, at time of compilation it uses compiler, at time of execution stage, it uses intrepreter
      JVM will run byte code, inside JVM iterpreter available

-JVM(Java Virtual Machine): JVM is part of JRE
--------------------------
-JVM is responsible for executing Java Programs
-JVM will allocate memory required for program execution(ie why java is called dynamic programming language) and deallocate when it is not
used. that's why Java is robust.
-It will convert byte code into machine understandable code
-Java is platform independent but JVM is not.

